(ned -- A ZERO DETECTION against the puck side wall, operator spec 2026-08-03)
(Model: puck = vertical cylinder, axis through the measured centre, top face)
(at the measured Z, 1 inch tall. A vertical rod touches the wall at the SAME)
(Y no matter how deep it probes. A TILTED rod does not: the touch Y shifts by)
(depth x tan A. So two plunge depths give the tilt directly.)
(Sequence, operator spec: touch top, touch bottom, CORRECT, touch bottom,)
(touch top -- if the spread did not shrink the math/sign is wrong, so ABORT)
(LOUDLY rather than iterate on a bad correction.)
(Reports DELTA Y BEFORE and DELTA Y AFTER. Applies the A rotation; writes NO)
(zero and NO offsets -- setting A's zero is a separate, explicit step.)
(Results: #3050 = dY before, #3051 = dY after, #3052 = A correction applied.)

o<cal_a_zero> sub
  #<cx>    = #1        (setter centre X, work frame -- from #3045)
  #<cy>    = #2        (setter centre Y, work frame -- from #3046)
  #<top>   = #3        (setter top Z, work frame -- from #3047)

  #<d_top> = 20.0      (shallow plunge below the top, operator spec)
  #<d_bot> = 50.0      (deep plunge below the top, operator spec)
  #<stand> = 30.0      (Y standoff from centre: outside puck + rod radius)
  #<reach> = 28.0      (max inward probe travel from the standoff)
  #<f_pr>  = 100.0     (probe feed)
  #<f_la>  = 10.0      (latch feed)
  #<f_tr>  = 500.0     (traverse)
  #<back>  = 1.0       (backoff before the latch)
  #<safe>  = 30.0      (Z clearance above the top for ANY A rotation)
  #<side>  = -1        (approach from -Y, probe toward +Y; flip to +1 to mirror)

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: no setter centre - run the centre calibration first)
  o6 endif

  M50 P0               (pin the feed override -- probes run at programmed feed)
  M64 P3               (puck UP)
  G4 P1.5

  (=== one wall touch at depth #<dep> -> #<ty> ==============================)
  (a call-free inline block: set #<dep>, then o<probe_wall> via the loop below)
  (implemented as a subroutine-in-file so both phases share EXACTLY one path)
  o100 sub
    (retract to hover, go to the standoff OUTSIDE the puck, then plunge)
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<f_tr>]
    G1 X#<cx> Y[#<cy> + #<side> * #<stand>] F[#<f_tr>]
    G1 Z[#<top> - #<dep>] F[#<f_tr>]

    (probe INWARD toward the axis; the wall stops us)
    G91
    G38.2 Y[0 - #<side> * #<reach>] F[#<f_pr>]
    o110 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      G90
      G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<f_tr>]
      M65 P3
      M50 P1
      (abort, CAL A: NO WALL at this depth - the modelled cylinder is only 25.4 mm tall, so a 50 mm plunge needs the body below the puck to share its diameter. Reduce d_bot or tell me the real geometry.)
    o110 endif
    G1 Y[#<side> * #<back>] F[#<f_tr>]
    G38.2 Y[0 - #<side> * [#<back> + 1]] F[#<f_la>]
    #<ty> = #5062

    (clear the wall)
    G1 Y[#<side> * 2] F[#<f_tr>]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<f_tr>]
  o100 endsub

  (=== BEFORE: touch top, then bottom =====================================)
  #<dep> = #<d_top>
  o100 call
  #<y_top_b> = #<ty>
  #<dep> = #<d_bot>
  o100 call
  #<y_bot_b> = #<ty>
  #<dy_b> = [#<y_bot_b> - #<y_top_b>]
  #3050 = #<dy_b>
  (PRINT, CAL A BEFORE: y at -20 = #<y_top_b>, y at -50 = #<y_bot_b>, DELTA Y = #<dy_b>)

  (=== CORRECT: tilt = atan(dY / dZ), dZ = the depth difference ============)
  #<dz>   = [#<d_bot> - #<d_top>]
  #<tilt> = [ATAN[#<dy_b>] / [#<dz>]]
  #<corr> = [0 - #<tilt>]        (one sign; the recheck below proves it)
  #3052 = #<corr>
  (PRINT, CAL A: tilt #<tilt> deg over #<dz> mm -> rotating A by #<corr> deg)

  o120 if [ABS[#<corr>] GT 5.0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<f_tr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL A: computed correction over 5 deg - refusing to swing the head that far on one measurement)
  o120 endif

  (rotate ONLY with the rod clear above the puck)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<f_tr>]
  G91
  G1 A#<corr> F600
  G90

  (=== AFTER: bottom first, then top (operator spec order) ================)
  #<dep> = #<d_bot>
  o100 call
  #<y_bot_a> = #<ty>
  #<dep> = #<d_top>
  o100 call
  #<y_top_a> = #<ty>
  #<dy_a> = [#<y_bot_a> - #<y_top_a>]
  #3051 = #<dy_a>
  (PRINT, CAL A AFTER: y at -50 = #<y_bot_a>, y at -20 = #<y_top_a>, DELTA Y = #<dy_a>)

  (=== verdict ============================================================)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<f_tr>]
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<f_tr>]
  M65 P3
  M50 P1

  o130 if [ABS[#<dy_a>] LT ABS[#<dy_b>]]
    (PRINT, CAL A OK: DELTA Y #<dy_b> -> #<dy_a> mm, A moved #<corr> deg. Sign is correct.)
    (DEBUG, CAL A: dY before #<dy_b>, after #<dy_a>, A corrected #<corr> deg)
  o130 else
    (DEBUG, CAL A FAILED: dY before #<dy_b>, after #<dy_a> - got WORSE. Flip side or the correction sign.)
    (abort, CAL A: correction made it WORSE (dY #<dy_b> -> #<dy_a>). The math or the sign is wrong -- flip #<corr> sign. Failing loudly by design.)
  o130 endif

o<cal_a_zero> endsub

M2 (end program)
